  "dreamlist.lucid": "Lucid dreaming means knowing that you are dreaming while you dream. Signs you are close: vivid dreams, remembering several dreams a night, sometimes thinking «this is strange».\nReality checks: several times a day, ask «am I dreaming?» and test it — look at your hands, read a text twice, or try to breathe with your nose pinched. In a dream these often fail.\nDream journal: write every dream as soon as you wake. Within weeks you will notice your own «dream signs».\nBefore sleep (MILD): repeat «next time I dream, I will know I am dreaming» and imagine noticing it.\nWake back to bed: wake up after about five hours of sleep, stay up for 15–20 minutes, then go back to sleep with that intention.\nWhen you become lucid, stay calm: rub your hands or look at the ground to stay in the dream.\nNever give up sleep for it: good, regular sleep matters more than any technique.",
  "dreamlist.lucid_ex": "Do five reality checks today and look at your hands each time.\nWrite down every dream you remember this morning, even one image.\nChoose a «dream sign» from your journal and look for it today.\nTonight, before sleep, repeat ten times: «I will know when I am dreaming».\nEvery time you go through a door today, ask: «am I dreaming?»\nRead a line of text, look away, and read it again — would it change in a dream?\nGo to bed at the same time tonight and wake slowly tomorrow.\nDraw one scene from a recent dream.\nSet one intention for your next dream: a place you would like to visit.\nAvoid screens for the last half hour before sleep tonight.\nWhen you wake tonight, stay still for a minute and replay your dream.\nAsk yourself three times today: «how did I get here?»\nTell someone one of your dreams; saying it helps memory.\nKeep a pen and paper by the bed tonight.",
  "dreamlist.m_airplane": "Big plans and goals taking off; travel or a change of perspective.",
  "dreamlist.m_angel": "Protection, guidance and hope.",
  "dreamlist.m_baby": "A new beginning, a fresh idea or a project that needs your care.",
  "dreamlist.m_bee": "Hard work and community; honey: sweet rewards.",
