  "sec.d_antiads": "Stops advertisers and tabchi (spam accounts): a new member's first link, contact or channel forward; the same ad posted in other Aegis groups; ad phrases with a contact.",
  "sec.d_antilink": "Stops links even when disguised: full-width letters, look-alike dots, “site dot com”, links on buttons. The «Allowed links» list and links to this group are fine.",
  "sec.d_captcha": "Newcomers are muted until they press the right button. Unsolved in time: kicked (or banned, or kept muted). With join requests the captcha goes to their private chat and decides the request.",
  "sec.d_flood": "Stops message floods: too many messages in a short time, or the same message again and again.",
  "sec.d_quarantine": "Newcomers can only send text (or nothing) for a while after joining. Telegram lifts it by itself when the time is up.",
  "sec.d_raid": "Notices a raid — many joins at once — and switches on raid mode for a while: a captcha or quarantine for newcomers, an emergency lock, or just an alert.",
  "sec.d_risk": "Adds up the signals of a message or a newcomer into a score, explains it, alerts the admins and acts above the threshold. ✅/❌ on each alert teaches the weights for this group.",
  "sec.d_shared": "When someone joins: were they banned or removed in other groups that use Aegis in the last 90 days? Then Aegis acts as set below and tells the admins. Only Aegis's own records are used; the CAS list is not checked (its API now needs a key).",
